# The Content Area 📏

The `width` and `height` properties set dimensions for an element's content area.

```css_not
.box {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  min-width: 200px;
  max-width: 100%; /* Prevents horizontal overflow on mobile screens! */
}
```

## Min and Max Constraints:
- `max-width: 100%`: Allows the box to shrink on smaller screens while never exceeding its set max width.
- `min-height`: Guarantees a minimum height while expanding dynamically if content overflows.

# Padding: Internal Spacing 🧘

Padding adds space between the content and the border. Background colors and images extend into the padding!

## Shorthand Syntax:
```css_not
/* 4 values: Top Right Bottom Left (Clockwise!) */
padding: 10px 20px 15px 5px;

/* 3 values: Top  Horizontal  Bottom */
padding: 10px 20px 15px;

/* 2 values: Vertical  Horizontal */
padding: 12px 24px;

/* 1 value: All 4 sides equal */
padding: 16px;
```

Individual properties: `padding-top`, `padding-right`, `padding-bottom`, `padding-left`.

# Borders 🖼️

The border wraps directly around the padding.

```css_not
/* Shorthand: border: [width] [style] [color] */
.card {
  border: 2px solid #cbd5e1;
  border-radius: 8px; /* Rounds the corners */
}
```

## Border Styles:
- `solid`, `dashed`, `dotted`, `double`, `none`

## Individual Side Borders:
```css_not
.header {
  border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0; /* Underline divider */
}
```

# Margin: External Separation 🏃

Margin creates space outside the element, pushing away adjacent elements.

```css_not
.alert {
  margin: 16px 0; /* 16px top and bottom, 0 left and right */
}
```

## Centering with Auto Margins:
For block-level elements with a defined width, `margin: 0 auto` automatically centers the box horizontally!

```css_not
.container {
  width: 80%;
  max-width: 1200px;
  margin: 0 auto; /* Equal margins left and right centers the container */
}
```

# The Modern Hero: `border-box` 🛡️

When using `box-sizing: border-box`, `width` sets the **total visible width**, including padding and border!

```css_not
.solution {
  box-sizing: border-box;
  width: 300px;
  padding: 20px;
  border: 5px solid blue;
}
```

## Total Rendered Width:
**Exactly 300px!** The browser automatically compresses the inner content area to 250px so the total width remains exactly 300px.

```css_not
/* The Essential Universal Reset */
*, *::before, *::after {
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
```

# Negative Margins ⬅️

Margins can have negative values (e.g. `-10px`, `-2rem`).

```css_not
.overlap-image {
  margin-top: -40px; /* Pulls the image 40px upward over the previous section */
}

.full-bleed {
  margin-left: -20px;
  margin-right: -20px; /* Expands element outside parent padding */
}
```

Negative margins pull elements closer or overlap them with adjacent elements.

# Display: `inline-block` 🌟

The best of both worlds! `inline-block` flows along horizontally like text, while respecting full box model dimensions:

```css_not
.tag-badge {
  display: inline-block;
  width: 120px;
  height: 36px;
  padding: 6px 12px;
  margin: 4px;
  background-color: #e0e7ff;
  border-radius: 9999px;
  text-align: center;
}
```

- Flows side-by-side with other inline elements.
- Fully respects `width`, `height`, vertical `padding`, and vertical `margin`!

# Outline vs Border ⭕

While `border` occupies space in the box model, `outline` is drawn **outside** the border without taking up any space!

```css_not
button:focus-visible {
  outline: 3px solid #3b82f6;
  outline-offset: 2px; /* Leaves a gap between border and outline */
}
```

## Why Outline is Essential for Accessibility:
Because outlines don't affect layout dimensions, adding a focus outline when a user tabs into a button never causes the surrounding layout to shift or jerk!

# Box Shadows (`box-shadow`) 🌫️

Add depth and elevation to boxes using `box-shadow`:

```css_not
/* Syntax: box-shadow: [offset-x] [offset-y] [blur-radius] [spread] [color] */
.card-elevated {
  box-shadow: 0 10px 15px -3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1),
              0 4px 6px -4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
}

/* Inner shadow */
.inset-panel {
  box-shadow: inset 0 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
}
```

# Real-World Component: Pricing Card 💳

```html_not
<div class="pricing-card">
  <h3>Pro Plan</h3>
  <p class="price">$29<span>/mo</span></p>
  <button>Choose Plan</button>
</div>
```

```css_not
.pricing-card {
  box-sizing: border-box;
  width: 280px;
  padding: 32px 24px;
  margin: 16px auto;
  border: 2px solid #e2e8f0;
  border-radius: 16px;
  background-color: #ffffff;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);
  text-align: center;
}

.price {
  font-size: 2.5rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  margin: 16px 0 24px;
}
```
